issue_context.body:
The long deprecated `server.connections` property is still being used in a number of places in our test suite. For instance, in `test\parallel\test-net-stream.js` 👍 

```js
// ...
s.server = new net.Server();
s.server.connections = 10;
s._server = s.server;

assert.strictEqual(s.server.connections, 10);
s.destroy();
assert.strictEqual(s.server.connections, 9);
s.destroy();
assert.strictEqual(s.server.connections, 9);
// ...
```

The replacement `server.getConnections()` is an asynchronous function. In some number of cases in our tests, we check that `server.connections === 0` within a `process.on('exit')` handler so the `server.getConnections()` API cannot be used as a direct replacement. Before we can move `server.connections` to End-of-Life, we need to figure out the right way to replace our own uses in the test suite.
